 "text": "Hey, nice to hear from you. How are you? Try cleaning both sides of the derailer hook with wet ear cleaner. A little dirt can stop it from grabbing. Sure, go ahead. Okay, it' being carefully tended to. Now, back to your slipping chain. Cleaned it, and it still skips. Turn it right only a few degrees, and shift it several times. If it starts to work nicely, stop there. Then the rear wheel needs a clean and maybe a little lube. Pop it off the bike and spin it in your hand. It should spin for long time without stopping.",
